    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d646">

                <pb facs="0773" n="1607" xml:id="pg1607"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 654.119/163</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-01T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 1, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1709. For Dresel [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 1. Legation’s 2929, March 24. Board approves the new agreement on exportation
                    of cotton. It should be stated, however, that we have no embargo on cotton into
                    Switzerland but must adhere to the ration figure of our agreement. Concerning
                    possibility of affording market here for cotton goods, etc., our reply will
                    follow later.</p>
                <p>Beginning now Board will number serially all cables for you and it is suggested
                    you do likewise.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
